cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sounding Line"
message: "If you use this instrument or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Haskins
    given-names: Abraham
    name-suffix: PhD
repository-code: "https://github.com/EmotiveAutomaton/sounding-line"
abstract: >-
  An instrument for reading intent out of real artifacts. Not an AI detector — an intent
  detector. It imposes a bounded, human-shaped hypothesis family over what an artifact was made
  for and measures fit inside it, reporting four quantities jointly: fit, convergence, depth, and
  the posterior that the intended reader was not a person. The instrument never makes a claim
  about authorship. Offshoot of the Ghost Scale Simulation.
keywords:
  - intent inference
  - inverse planning
  - artifact provenance
  - corpus quality
  - LLM grooming
  - AI text detection
license: MIT
